---
// Experience.astro — Professional work history (newest-first)
// Four employers: FSCPay, AT&T (with three progressive roles), Tannery Row, Glimpse
---

<section class="experience">
  <p class="section-moral">
    <em>The ant that shipped in winter had been building since spring.</em>
  </p>

  <h2 id="experience">Experience</h2>

  <div class="employers-grid">
    <!-- AT&T: People Analytics (Software Engineer → Senior Software Engineer) -->
    <article class="employer-card">
      <div class="employer-header">
        <h3>AT&T</h3>
        <span class="employer-duration">Nov 2021 – Jun 2025 · 3 yrs 8 mos</span>
      </div>
      <p class="employer-location">Chicago, IL · People Analytics</p>

      <div class="roles-list">
        <div class="role">
          <div class="role-header">
            <h4>Software Engineer → Senior Software Engineer, People Analytics</h4>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <ul class="role-bullets">
        <li>Hired through AT&T's Technology Development Program onto People Analytics, a startup-style HR team building full-stack reporting products on the HR DataHub (Java/Spring Boot, Angular, Azure — millions of rows of sensitive employee data); promoted to Senior within the first year.</li>
        <li>Shipped the PLE reporting tool for enterprise learning data — <strong>1M+ reports delivered per year</strong> — and built stochastic workforce-modeling tools for HR planning.</li>
        <li>Designed <strong>HRMAN</strong>, a company-wide RBAC service grown from the team's user/role logic, serving tool-access control and real-time reporting-data authorization to teams across AT&T.</li>
        <li>Initiated and led <strong>"Canned Reporting"</strong>: a config-driven reporting platform where report definitions live in the database over one generic frontend and backend; built the POC APIs and ran live demos of report creation, RBAC integration, and compound reports on a Java task-executor pool.</li>
        <li>Rearchitected backend cross-cutting concerns with Spring AOP — argument resolvers and exception handlers reduced authn/authz to a single annotation; rebuilt low-level result-set processing for a <strong>40% memory reduction</strong>; introduced Redis caching to the team.</li>
        <li>Grew the team from 5 to 12 developers as its first TDP — recruited through the program, mentored new hires, and wrote the onboarding guide that cut developer ramp-up from 3 days to 1.</li>
        <li>Owned production releases and observability: Azure Application Insights monitoring saved ~20 developer-hours a month; served 8 months as Senior Scrum Master, lifting team velocity 27%.</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="employer-tags">
        <span class="tag">Java</span>
        <span class="tag">Spring Boot</span>
        <span class="tag">Angular</span>
        <span class="tag">Azure</span>
        <span class="tag">Vertica</span>
        <span class="tag">Redis</span>
        <span class="tag">RBAC</span>
      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- Post-AT&T trajectory -->
    <article class="employer-card trajectory-bridge">
      <p class="trajectory-note">
        <em>Since AT&T: independent automation-systems engineering — client delivery systems and the aesop orchestration harness.</em>
      </p>
    </article>

    <!-- FSCPay: Technical Cofounder + Lead Software Engineer -->
    <article class="employer-card">
      <div class="employer-header">
        <h3>FSCPay</h3>
        <span class="employer-duration">Oct 2025 – Present</span>
      </div>
      <p class="employer-location">Chicago, IL</p>

      <div class="roles-list">
        <div class="role">
          <div class="role-header">
            <h4>Technical Cofounder</h4>
            <span class="role-duration">Self-employed, Oct 2025 – Present</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="role">
          <div class="role-header">
            <h4>Lead Software Engineer</h4>
            <span class="role-duration">Freelance, Aug 2025 – Present · Remote</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <ul class="role-bullets">
        <li>Designed and developed payment solutions for FSCPay, a fintech startup.</li>
        <li>Led backend development utilizing LLM intelligence APIs to enhance payment processing.</li>
        <li>Collaborated with cross-functional teams to ensure seamless integration of payment systems.</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="employer-tags">
        <span class="tag">Java</span>
      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- The Tannery Row: Technology & Operations Lead -->
    <article class="employer-card">
      <div class="employer-header">
        <h3>The Tannery Row</h3>
        <span class="employer-duration">Dec 2018 – Present · 5 yrs 8 mos</span>
      </div>
      <p class="employer-location">Chicago, IL · On-site</p>

      <div class="roles-list">
        <div class="role">
          <div class="role-header">
            <h4>Technology & Operations Lead</h4>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <ul class="role-bullets">
        <li>Proposed and launched the company's leather sample-book product line, then scaled it into the full-time program I run today — engineering the swatch-book and leather-panel manufacturing processes and managing staff.</li>
        <li>Engineered a Google Tag Manager <strong>"backend" for a backend-less Squarespace store</strong>: dynamic ads, organic listings, and a product-feed API built by treating page visits as tag-firing events through Google's own infrastructure; maintained to this day — online sales <strong>+10% YoY</strong>.</li>
        <li>Own SEO end to end: grew organic Google traffic to rival direct traffic for the first time in company history; online sales rose <strong>24% in my first three months back</strong>.</li>
        <li>Built <strong>ECM-ai</strong>, an accounting tool that gamifies repairing bad order data so invoices import cleanly (a daily manual job became a monthly automated one), and <strong>TRTools</strong>, an internal RBAC-gated automation toolbox for all employees.</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="employer-tags">
        <span class="tag">Google Tag Manager</span>
        <span class="tag">Squarespace</span>
        <span class="tag">SEO</span>
        <span class="tag">Python</span>
        <span class="tag">RBAC</span>
      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- Glimpse: UI/UX Developer & Co-Founder -->
    <article class="employer-card">
      <div class="employer-header">
        <h3>Glimpse</h3>
        <span class="employer-duration">2014 – 2018 · 4 yrs</span>
      </div>
      <p class="employer-location">Illinois</p>

      <div class="roles-list">
        <div class="role">
          <div class="role-header">
            <h4>UI/UX Developer & Co-Founder</h4>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <ul class="role-bullets">
        <li>Built and released the social media app <strong>"Glimpse"</strong> (Swift); won <strong>best in Illinois in the Verizon Innovative App Challenge</strong> and pitched the app to live audiences and investors — later rebranded and sold after my departure.</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="employer-tags">
        <span class="tag">Swift</span>
        <span class="tag">iOS</span>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .experience {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: var(--width-container);
    margin: 0 auto var(--space-20);
    padding: var(--space-12) var(--space-8);
  }

  /* Override shared section h2 */
  .experience h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-3xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }

  .employers-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-8);
    margin-top: var(--space-10);
  }

  /* Employer card styling */
  .employer-card {
    background-color: var(--color-bg-secondary);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: var(--space-6);
    transition: border-color var(--duration-base) var(--ease-in-out),
                background-color var(--duration-base) var(--ease-in-out);
  }

  .employer-card:hover {
    border-color: var(--accent);
    background-color: var(--color-bg);
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .employer-card {
      transition: none;
    }
  }

  /* Employer header: company name + total duration */
  .employer-header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .employer-header h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin: 0;
    line-height: var(--leading-tight);
  }

  .employer-duration {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  /* Employer location */
  .employer-location {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-tertiary);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4) 0;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wide);
  }

  /* Roles list container */
  .roles-list {
    margin: var(--space-4) 0 var(--space-6) 0;
  }

  /* Individual role */
  .role {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-5);
  }

  .role:last-child {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  /* Role header: title + duration */
  .role-header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .role-header h4 {
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .role-duration {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--color-text-tertiary);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  /* Role context (e.g., "Hybrid", "Remote") */
  .role-context {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--color-text-tertiary);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wide);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3) 0;
  }

  /* Role description (used for Tannery Row pointer) */
  .role-description {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
    margin: var(--space-4) 0 0 0;
  }

  /* Role bullets */
  .role-bullets {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4) 0;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
  }

  .role-bullets li {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
    padding-left: var(--space-4);
    position: relative;
  }

  .role-bullets li::before {
    content: '•';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  /* Employer tags */
  .employer-tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    margin-top: var(--space-5);
  }

  .tag {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    background-color: var(--color-code-bg);
    color: var(--color-code-text);
    padding: var(--space-1) var(--space-2);
    border-radius: 2px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wide);
  }

  .trajectory-bridge {
    background-color: transparent;
    border: none;
    padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-6);
    text-align: center;
    min-height: auto;
  }

  .trajectory-bridge:hover {
    background-color: transparent;
    border: none;
  }

  .trajectory-note {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    font-style: italic;
    margin: 0;
    line-height: var(--leading-normal);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
  }

  /* Responsive adjustments */
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .experience {
      padding: var(--space-8) var(--space-4);
    }

    .employer-card {
      padding: var(--space-5) var(--space-4);
    }

    .employer-header {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: flex-start;
    }

    .employer-duration {
      white-space: normal;
    }

    .role-header {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: flex-start;
    }

    .role-duration {
      white-space: normal;
    }

    .employer-tags {
      gap: var(--space-2);
    }
  }
</style>
